            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to get tangled, then the Hindi for to raise (a topic)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आपत्ति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आपत्ति — āpatti — \"an objection\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मुझे तुम्हारे विचार पर कोई आपत्ति नहीं है। mujhe tumhāre vicār par koī āpatti nahīṃ hai. I have no objection to your idea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आपत्ति (āpatti) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit āpatti, \"an occurrence; a mishap\" (Monier-Williams). Monier-Williams does not give the sense of an objection, which is a later Hindi one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
