          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फुसलाना — phuslānā — \"to coax, to wheedle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बच्चा दवा नहीं पी रहा था, इसलिए माँ ने उसे फुसलाया। baccā davā nahīṃ pī rahā thā, isliye māṁ ne use phuslāyā. The child wouldn't take the medicine, so his mother coaxed him."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने बच्चे को फुसलाया, usne bacce ko phuslāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फुसलाना (phuslānā) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit spṛśati, \"touches\" (CDIAL 13815). CDIAL lists the Hindi verb, \"to cajole\", under this entry; the step from touching to coaxing is not spelled out there."
            }
          ]
        },
